Downloading rsna-intracranial-hemorrhage-detection.zip to data/rsna



=== rsna ===
Official RSNA 2019 challenge data (manuscript ref [27]). Requires accepting the competition rules on kaggle.com first (one-time, logged-in click) before the API download works. ~450GB uncompressed -- budget disk space and time.

$ kaggle competitions download -c rsna-intracranial-hemorrhage-detection -p data/rsna
  unzipping rsna-intracranial-hemorrhage-detection.zip ...
  done -- leaving rsna-intracranial-hemorrhage-detection.zip in place in case you need to re-extract; delete it manually once you've verified the extracted contents.

=== PhysioNet-ICH (manuscript ref [29]) is NOT downloaded by this script ===
It is restricted-access: register at https://physionet.org, sign the Restricted Health Data Use Agreement (v1.5.0), then download manually from https://physionet.org/content/ct-ich/1.3.1/ into data/physionet_ich. Start this today if you haven't already -- the approval step, not the download itself, is what takes time.

Next: point each ich_gen loader at data/<name> and read that loader's 'SCHEMA ASSUMPTION' docstring before trusting its output against what you actually downloaded (see code/README.md's 'Getting the data' section).
